WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.905
Many organizations generate SBOMs during software builds, release processes, and deployment activities.

2
00:00:06.905 --> 00:00:13.729
Integrating SBOM generation into development workflows can improve consistency and reduce manual effort.

3
00:00:13.729 --> 00:00:25.104
The software development lifecycle is a natural place to create SBOMs because build systems often know which packages, libraries, containers, and artifacts were included in a release.

4
00:00:25.104 --> 00:00:27.519
Automation helps keep SBOMs current.

5
00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:35.890
If an SBOM is generated every time software is built or released, the inventory is more likely to reflect what was actually delivered.

6
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.023
SBOMs can also be stored with release artifacts.

7
00:00:39.023 --> 00:00:44.511
This makes it easier to connect a product version to the components that were present at the time of release.

8
00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:48.412
Development teams can use SBOMs to review dependency changes.

9
00:00:48.412 --> 00:00:56.045
A new package, major version change, or unexpected transitive dependency may deserve additional review before release.

10
00:00:56.045 --> 00:01:02.451
Security teams can use SBOM outputs to enrich vulnerability management and software risk workflows.

11
00:01:02.451 --> 00:01:08.747
Compliance teams may use the same data to support evidence requests or customer assurance processes.

12
00:01:08.747 --> 00:01:14.524
The practical lesson is to make SBOM generation part of how software is built and maintained.

13
00:01:14.524 --> 00:01:21.498
When SBOMs are embedded in the lifecycle, they become living operational artifacts rather than occasional documents.

14
00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:25.041
Teams should also decide how SBOMs are versioned and retained.

15
00:01:25.041 --> 00:01:34.200
Being able to connect a released product version to the SBOM generated for that release can be critical during vulnerability response or customer assurance work.

16
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.343
Lifecycle integration also makes ownership clearer.

17
00:01:37.343 --> 00:01:48.907
If each product team knows where its SBOMs are created, stored, and reviewed, software transparency becomes a repeatable engineering practice rather than an occasional special request.
